  "notes": "CONJUGATION: {佇|たたず}む is a godan verb (む row). Te-form: {佇|たたず}んで.\n\nUSAGE: A literary, somewhat poetic word that evokes a quiet, still image. More expressive than simply ⟦{立|た}つ→立つ：00758_tatsu⟧ (to stand). Often used in novels, poetry, and descriptive writing to create atmosphere.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{窓辺|まどべ}→窓辺：20444_madobe⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧{佇|たたず}む (to stand by the window)\n- ⟦{佇|たたず}まい→佇まい：09178_tatazumai⟧ (appearance, bearing, atmosphere of a place)\n\nRELATED: The noun ⟦{佇|たたず}まい→佇まい：09178_tatazumai⟧ means the overall appearance, atmosphere, or bearing of a place or person, and is very commonly used.",
